WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.160
The original run of Twin Peaks is something
that feels entirely unique to me.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.270
Even decades later, after countless other
shows have been influenced by or ripped off

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.920
various elements of Twin Peaks, there’s
something there that nobody has recreated

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:22.550
in quite the same way David Lynch and Mark
Frost managed to in the early 90’s.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.140
When I heard that Twin Peaks was returning,
I was excited and intrigued, and a little

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.780
worried.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.579
What would the return of Twin Peaks look like?

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:40.070
Are the things that Lynch and Frost care about
and want to continue on the same things that

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.949
fans of the show care about?

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:46.769
And as Twin Peaks: The Return unfolds, I think
we can begin to answer that question.

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:49.629
I’m Thomas Flight.

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:52.550
Thank you to Squarespace for sponsoring this
video.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:57.410
This video will contain images from all seasons
of Twin Peaks, but I’ll try to avoid major

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:04.409
plot spoilers.

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:08.470
Twin Peaks is a difficult show to talk about,
it’s hard to describe to people, and I find

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.010
it difficult to explain what it is I like
about the show.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:18.380
But there’s a word that seems to come up
again and again.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.460
Weird.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.690
Twin Peaks is weird.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.400
I don’t mean that in a negative sense.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.400
It’s weirdness catches you off guard.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.250
Much of it has a conventional facade laden
with soap opera tropes and drama, but as it

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:51.060
pulls you into what feels like normalcy, it
uncovers it’s strange underbelly.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.730
Part of what I think created the unique magic
of the original seasons was David Lynch’s

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.690
weirdness constrained by the necessity of
creating a network TV show.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:04.450
Lynch’s films are something amazing to experience,
and I enjoy when a director has free reign

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.460
over a project to do what they want.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.869
But sometimes something very interesting can
come out of a situation that puts constraint

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:12.230
on an artist.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:21.630
David Lynch had to make a TV show that the
network would allow him to air, the result

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:28.440
is a well made crime drama with a subtle foundation
of Lynch’s stylistic weirdness, while occasionally

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:34.880
the full force of his brand of weird breaks
through, creating the strangest tv show on

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.330
the air at the time.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.330
This brings us back to Twin Peaks The Return.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.700
As I watched the first several episodes of
the new season, I often found myself wondering,

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.100
what is Twin Peaks to David Lynch?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.500
In the new season, Lynch is unconstrained,
and some of the vibe that constituted what

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.819
I personally felt was “Twin Peaks” was
lost.

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:03.541
If the old show was 70% Network tv and 30%
full blown Lynch, the new season was 30% my

00:03:03.541 --> 00:03:07.270
idea of Twin Peaks and 70% full blown Lynch.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:12.250
Don’t get me wrong, as a fan of what I’m
calling “full blown David Lynch” I was

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.590
excited to be watching something different
and experimental.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:21.430
I might be missing a little of the campy,
soap opera vibe of the original seasons, but

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.270
I was excited to be watching Lynch do his
thing.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:37.530
Then I watched episode 8.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:44.440
I sat there, somewhat astounded that Showtime
actually allowed Lynch to air this on TV.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.490
And it hit me…

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.860
This is Twin Peaks.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:53.050
David Lynch wasn’t creating a new season
that would just give me more of the feelings

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:57.330
I have watching a 25 year old, campy and quirky
tv show.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:03.120
Whether it was his intention or not he was
creating a show that would give even a seasoned

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.980
viewer of modern TV the sort of experience
people had watching the original Twin Peaks

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.400
air.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.810
The original run of Twin Peaks was on after
shows like Cheers, viewers must have been

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:25.840
struck by the unique strangeness, some would
have asked “what the heck am I watching?”

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:40.150
But watching the original seasons of twin
peaks now doesn’t give you quite that experience,

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:44.250
you can still feel it’s weirdness years
later, but we’re so surrounded by other

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.831
shows that have similar levels of weirdness
in them, that the original weirdness of twin

00:04:48.831 --> 00:04:54.130
peaks doesn’t stand in as stark contrast
to everything around it anymore.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:05:00.440
But Twin Peaks, is once again with it’s
return, decades later, probably the strangest

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.580
thing to ever air on TV.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.960
David Lynch continues to push the boundaries,
to tell stories how he wants to tell them,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.970
not how they should be told.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.220
I don’t want to be reductive.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.500
I’m not saying twin peaks is only “Weird”
or that it only pushes boundaries.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.479
But when I was anticipating the new season,
pushing the boundaries of storytelling is

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:25.750
an element of the show that I had overlooked
in my anticipation about being reunited with

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.270
old characters and old storylines being concluded.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:41.169
And I don’t think Lynch’s goal is simply
to be weird either, in Twin Peaks a significant

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:46.040
theme is characters encountering things that
are or appear otherworldly.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:50.400
An important aspect of telling a story about
how people behave in the face of things they

00:05:50.400 --> 00:06:30.440
don’t understand is creating at least some
of those feelings within 

00:06:30.440 --> 00:07:03.289
the audience.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.889
This will inevitably turn some people away.

00:07:05.889 --> 00:07:10.850
I’m sure there may have been a drop in viewership
of the new season after episode 8, just as

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:14.060
viewership of the original seasons dropped
off.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:20.539
But if Twin Peaks was accessible, it may arguably
not be the same twin peaks.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:24.980
And as I go back over episodes of the new
season I’m seeing many of the ingredients

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.160
that made up the original Twin Peaks are present.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.310
Even if a lot of the plot takes place away
from the beloved little town, you can see

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:37.270
almost every element of what would make up
Twin Peaks the return watching the original

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.270
seasons.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.270
And I’ve come to realize that the weirdness
of Twin Peaks isn’t just a sideshow, it’s

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.270
fundamental to the experience.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.990
Twin Peaks The Return is a genre defying show
that plays the spectrum from goofy humor to

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.270
genuine psychological horror.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:50.880
And it expands on the world of Twin Peaks
in unpredictable and fascinating ways.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:56.430
The original twin peaks was a singular, interesting,
influential creation.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:05.600
And I firmly believe that Twin Peaks: The
Return is as well.

